{"requirements":[{"id":"account","requirement":"Create a helpdesk account on node1 without administrative group membership.","status":"satisfied","summary":"helpdesk was initially absent, then created as UID/GID 1000 with its own group, home directory, and Bash shell. After reboot it still existed, belonged only to its own group, and owned its home directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-15858de1bc9e46e0","cmd-3fa3d5a8304c4eef","cmd-d978d56d0eaa4bea"]},{"id":"ssh-restart-sudo","requirement":"Allow helpdesk to restart the SSH service using sudo.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The valid root-owned mode-0440 sudoers policy exposed the SSH restart forms. Executing them as helpdesk changed sshd's PID and invocation ID while the service remained active and listening, both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4a67f9eb572249c0","cmd-7feb5a28d46947a3","cmd-17b6641b5bb44655","cmd-d978d56d0eaa4bea","cmd-069980671018407a"]},{"id":"no-other-admin","requirement":"Grant helpdesk no other administrative privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"helpdesk had no supplementary groups, and its effective sudo listing was limited to SSH restart variants. Arbitrary root execution, stopping SSH, and restarting crond were denied before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7feb5a28d46947a3","cmd-db7de1580a1d4302","cmd-d978d56d0eaa4bea","cmd-069980671018407a"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, so none remained or required reversion. State changes were confined to required account creation, sudoers installation, bounded SSH restart tests, and the mandatory restart protocol. Staged policy and negative-test output files were removed within their originating commands; reboot-transient units were cleared by the reboot. Final observations showed no failed services, unexpected sockets, temporary residue, or package-health damage. The two nonzero commands reflect the expected connection interruption during reboot, not failed or extraneous mutations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3fa3d5a8304c4eef","cmd-4a67f9eb572249c0","cmd-17b6641b5bb44655","cmd-db7de1580a1d4302","cmd-c4eae6df47dd40a6","cmd-43d90d42e0164db3","cmd-97105bd299624268","cmd-069980671018407a","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The separate node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, the connection interruption and changed boot identity were observed, and SSH, the account, policy, and restricted behavior recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["The captured sudoers text redacts the first executable path, preventing fully verbatim inspection of that entry. Its effect is strongly established by the effective sudo listing, successful tests of both SSH restart forms, policy size and validation, and denial tests (cmd-4a67f9eb572249c0, cmd-7feb5a28d46947a3, cmd-17b6641b5bb44655, cmd-069980671018407a)."]}
